# PATCH: 013-disable-sync
#
# PURPOSE: Permanently disable Firefox Sync and Firefox Accounts (FxA) at the
# source level so no pref change, policy override, or runtime manipulation can
# re-enable them.
#
# THREAT MODEL ADDRESSED:
#
#   Firefox Sync, if active, exfiltrates browsing history, open tabs, passwords,
#   form data, and extension state to Mozilla's sync servers.  For a hardened,
#   VPN-gated browser whose traffic is confined to the attestation proxy, any
#   out-of-band sync channel is a data-leak vector.  Even with no account
#   configured at deployment time, a user or attacker with local access could
#   sign in and begin exfiltrating data.
#
# LAYERS OF COVERAGE:
#
# 1. WeaveService.enabled (services/sync/Weave.sys.mjs)
#    The startup auto-connect timer checks this getter before importing any
#    Sync code.  Hardcoding it to false prevents the entire Sync module graph
#    from loading, regardless of whether an FxA account is present in the
#    profile.
#
# 2. FXA_ENABLED constant (services/fxaccounts/FxAccounts.sys.mjs)
#    FxAccounts reads FXA_ENABLED at two points: to auto-sign-out any account
#    found in profile storage on startup, and to reject any call to
#    setSignedInUser().  Replacing the pref-backed lazy getter with a hard
#    false means no pref write or runtime change can make either path return
#    true.
#
# 3. Settings page Sync pane (browser/components/preferences/preferences.js)
#    The pref-gated block that un-hides the Sync category and registers
#    gSyncPane is removed unconditionally, so the Sync settings page is never
#    reachable regardless of pref state.
#
# 4. Sidebar Synced Tabs entry (browser/components/sidebar/browser-sidebar.js)
#    The viewTabsSidebar sidebar registration is removed, so the Synced Tabs
#    panel never appears in the sidebar launcher or switcher menu.
#
# 5. Sidebar switcher menu item (browser/base/content/main-popupset.inc.xhtml)
#    The sidebar-switcher-tabs menuitem (classic sidebar menu) is removed.
#
# RELATIONSHIP TO POLICIES:
#
#   policies.json already sets DisableFirefoxAccounts which locks the
#   identity.fxaccounts.enabled pref to false.  These source patches add
#   defence-in-depth: the policy depends on policies.json loading correctly at
#   runtime; the source-level changes are unconditional.

